          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            A desiccant dehumidifier is a cold-weather specialist. In a garage, boat, cabin or unheated room that spends the damp season below about 60°F, it keeps removing water when a compressor unit has frosted up and stopped. For most of those spaces the Ivation 19-pint is the one to buy, with the 13-pint for closets and small cabins and the Eva-Dry where quiet matters most.
          </p>
